---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import colibri from "../../assets/colibri-homepage.png";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colibri Physical Therapy Case Study — Vitaliy Bernatskyy"
  description="A responsive physical therapy website with a welcoming visual identity, clear service information, and an accessible visit-request flow."
>
  <article class="case-study">
    <header class="case-hero shell">
      <a class="back-link" href="/#work">← All work</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Business website · Design & development</p>
      <h1>Colibri Physical Therapy</h1>
      <p class="case-intro">A welcoming website that helps visitors understand a practice’s services, get to know their therapist, and take the first step toward a visit.</p>
      <dl class="case-facts">
        <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Website design & development</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Project</dt><dd>Physical therapy website</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Core stack</dt><dd>HTML · CSS · JavaScript · EmailJS</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <div class="case-visual shell">
      <img src={colibri.src} alt="Colibri Physical Therapy homepage showing the Move freely. Live fully. headline, hummingbird imagery, and Request a visit button" width={colibri.width} height={colibri.height} />
    </div>

    <section class="case-section shell" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
      <p class="section-index">01 / THE CHALLENGE</p>
      <div class="case-section-body">
        <h2 id="challenge-title">Make the first step feel approachable.</h2>
        <p class="case-lede">Visitors need to understand the care on offer and how to get started.</p>
        <p>
          The site brings services, a therapist introduction, the visit process, and common questions into one clear page. Repeated “Request a visit” buttons give visitors a way to get in touch wherever they are in that journey.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="section-index">02 / THE EXPERIENCE</p>
        <h2>From a first impression to a conversation.</h2>
        <div class="architecture-flow" aria-label="Website visitor journey">
          <div><span>01</span><h3>Explore the practice</h3><p>A hummingbird identity, soft greens, and generous spacing establish the visual tone alongside a clear introduction to the services.</p></div>
          <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <div><span>02</span><h3>Understand the next steps</h3><p>The therapist profile, visit process, and expandable FAQs help visitors find answers before reaching out.</p></div>
          <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <div><span>03</span><h3>Request a visit</h3><p>A contact dialog collects basic details. The practice can follow up to discuss the visit and share a scheduling link.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section shell" aria-labelledby="decisions-title">
      <p class="section-index">03 / KEY DECISIONS</p>
      <div class="case-section-body">
        <h2 id="decisions-title">Simple pages, thoughtful interactions.</h2>
        <div class="decision-list">
          <article><span>Visual identity</span><h3>Carry the brand through the page</h3><p>The hummingbird mark and hero imagery work with serif headings and a green palette to create a consistent, welcoming presentation.</p></article>
          <article><span>Responsive layout</span><h3>Keep information easy to scan</h3><p>Desktop sections become a single column on smaller screens, with a collapsible menu and a visit-request form that fits the available space.</p></article>
          <article><span>Accessibility</span><h3>Support keyboard navigation</h3><p>A skip link, visible focus styles, native FAQ disclosures, and dialog focus management support navigation without a mouse. Reduced-motion preferences are respected.</p></article>
          <article><span>Contact flow</span><h3>Make request status clear</h3><p>The EmailJS integration includes validation, a pending state, success feedback, and an error message with an email fallback. The form asks visitors to save medical details for their therapist.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section case-reflection shell" aria-labelledby="result-title">
      <p class="section-index">04 / THE RESULT</p>
      <div class="case-section-body">
        <h2 id="result-title">A complete business website.</h2>
        <p class="case-lede">Service information and a practical contact flow come together in a responsive design.</p>
        <p>
          Built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, the website introduces the practice and guides visitors toward a conversation.
        </p>
        <div class="case-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/#contact">Discuss your website <span>→</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/#work">Explore more work <span>→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
